 "pdf_title": "64 ### 5.4 Juvenile Apprehended A total of 160919 juveniles and youthful offenders were arrested during 1978 and out of which 40·9 percent were arrested for committing crime under IPC. The highest number of arrests under IPC crimes were noticed under the crime head, 'Thefts' (17679) accounting for 26·9 percent of the total IPC crimes while 'Riots' (13854) accounted for 21.1 percent of total arrests. The arrests for crimes committed under local and special laws accounted for 59·2 percent of the total arrests. Two Acts viz., the 'Gambling Act' (23691) and the 'Prohibition Act' (25946) together accounted for 52·2 percent of the total arrests under the local and special laws. The relevant statistics may be seen in Table 35.",
